{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConcurrentChange","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"title":"runConcurrently(_:)","externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V15runConcurrentlyyySayAA16ConcurrentChangeVGF","extendedModule":"WorldModule","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Concurrency.swift#L159","fileName":"Concurrency.swift"},"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"Runs ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"text":" at the same time, each on a copy of the world, and keeps what each wrote.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changes","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ConcurrentChange"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each change reads the world as it was before any of them ran, and writes only the types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its access lists, so the result is the same as running them one after another in any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order. A change sees the components and resources other changes write as missing, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"must declare everything it reads.","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"c"}]},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"text":") besides the changes themselves, for ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"c"}]},{"text":" changes and ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"text":" stored","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity"},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No two accesses conflict. Each change writes only the component and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resource types its access lists, and spawns, despawns and changes the hierarchy not at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all; a change that writes another component type or changes the entities traps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/runConcurrently(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":